      <p class="lead">With quick-service prices facing sustained inflationary pressure across the United States, pulling into a Dairy Queen drive-thru and paying full retail price without tapping the mobile app is leaving serious money on the table. The official <strong>DQ® Rewards platform</strong> operates with a fixed accrual rate of 10 points per dollar spent. However, behind this simple user interface lies a massive disparity in reward valuations. Cashing in points for the wrong item cuts your effective rebate by more than 70%. <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu Research Desk</a> audited the entire 2026 rewards ledger to calculate the exact cent-per-point efficiency of every tier.</p>

      <h2>The Cent-Per-Point (CPP) Mathematical Valuation Ledger</h2>
      <p>In consumer finance, loyalty point programs are evaluated using <strong>Cent-Per-Point (CPP)</strong> metrics. Dividing the real-world retail value of a reward item by the required points reveals which redemptions maximize your purchasing power:</p>

